Distribute \(\sqrt{133}\) and simplify:
\[
(\sqrt{14}-\sqrt{65})\sqrt{133}
=\sqrt{1862}-\sqrt{8645}
=\sqrt{49\cdot38}-\sqrt{8645}
=\boxed{7\sqrt{38}-\sqrt{8645}}.
\]
Since \(8645=5\cdot7\cdot13\cdot19\), its radical cannot be simplified further.

