The RREF given is correct, but I compressed several elementary row operations into single steps. Here they are separately:

\[
\begin{pmatrix}
-5&-4&2&-9\\
8&-10&-5&5
\end{pmatrix}
\xrightarrow{R_1\leftarrow-\frac15R_1}
\begin{pmatrix}
1&\frac45&-\frac25&\frac95\\
8&-10&-5&5
\end{pmatrix}.
\]

Next, \(R_2\leftarrow R_2-8R_1\):
\[
\begin{pmatrix}
1&\frac45&-\frac25&\frac95\\
0&-\frac{82}{5}&-\frac95&-\frac{47}{5}
\end{pmatrix}.
\]

Scale \(R_2\leftarrow-\frac5{82}R_2\), then eliminate above its pivot using \(R_1\leftarrow R_1-\frac45R_2\):
\[
\boxed{
\begin{pmatrix}
1&0&-\frac{20}{41}&\frac{55}{41}\\
0&1&\frac9{82}&\frac{47}{82}
\end{pmatrix}
}.
\]
The leading entries are \(1\), and each pivot is the only nonzero entry in its column, so this is in reduced row echelon form.

