\end{array}
Step 2:
\begin{array}{l}
 \text{The }\text{standard }\text{deviation }\text{is }\text{given }\text{by}: \\
 \sqrt{(\text{variance})} \\
\end{array}
Step 3:
\begin{array}{l}
 \text{The }\text{(sample) }\text{variance }\text{of }\text{a }\text{list }\text{of }\text{numbers }X=\left\{X_1,X_2,\ldots ,X_n\right\} \text{with }\text{mean }\mu =\frac{X_1+X_2+\ldots +X

model_response:
The mean is \(\bar{x}=\frac{-14+6+6}{3}=-\frac23\).

The sample standard deviation is
\[
s=\sqrt{\frac{\sum (x_i-\bar{x})^2}{n-1}}
=\sqrt{\frac{(-40/3)^2+2(20/3)^2}{2}}
=\frac{20}{\sqrt3}
\approx \boxed{11.55}.
\]

