Step 3:
\begin{array}{l}
 \text{The }\text{(sample) }\text{variance }\text{of }\text{a }\text{list }\text{of }\text{numbers }X=\left\{X_1,X_2,\ldots ,X_n\right\} \text{with }\text{mean }\mu =\frac{X_1+X_2+\l

model_response:
The mean is \(\bar{x}=\frac{41}{6}\). Using the sample standard deviation formula,
\[
s=\sqrt{\frac{\sum x_i^2-n\bar{x}^{\,2}}{n-1}}
=\sqrt{\frac{603-6(41/6)^2}{5}}
=\sqrt{\frac{1937}{30}}
\approx \boxed{8.04}.
\]

