model_response:
Let \(A=\begin{pmatrix}-3&-3\\1&5\end{pmatrix}\). Since
\[
\det A=(-3)(5)-(-3)(1)=-12\ne0,
\]
its pseudoinverse equals its ordinary inverse:
\[
\boxed{A^{+}=A^{-1}
=\frac1{-12}\begin{pmatrix}5&3\\-1&-3\end{pmatrix}
=\begin{pmatrix}
-\frac5{12}&-\frac14\\[2pt]
\frac1{12}&\frac14
\end{pmatrix}.}
\]

