question:
Add the two matrices
$\left(
\begin{array}{ccc}
 -9 & -8 & 7 \\
 -7 & 7 & -8 \\
\end{array}
\right)$ and
$\left(
\begin{array}{ccc}
 3 & -2 & 5 \\
 -6 & -2 & 9 \\
\end{array}
\right)$

ground_truth:
Step 1:
\begin{array}{l}

\begin{array}{l}
 \text{Simplify the following}: \\
 \left(
\begin{array}{ccc}
 -9 & -8 & 7 \\
 -7 & 7 & -8 \\
\end{array}
Step 2:
\begin{array}{l}
 \left(
\begin{array}{ccc}
 -9 & -8 & 7 \\
 -7 & 7 & -8 \\
\end{array}
Step 3:
\begin{array}{l}
 -9+3=-6: \\
 \left(
\begin{array}{ccc}
 \fbox{$-6$} & -8-2 & 7+5 \\
 -7-6 & 7-2 & -8+9 \\
\end{array}
Step 4:
\begin{array}{l}
 -8-2=-(8+2): \\
 \left(
\begin{array}{ccc}
 -6 & \fbox{$-(8+2)$} & 7+5 \\
 -7-6 & 7-2 & -8+9 \\
\end

model_response:
\[
\begin{pmatrix}
-9+3 & -8-2 & 7+5\\
-7-6 & 7-2 & -8+9
\end{pmatrix}
=
\boxed{\begin{pmatrix}
-6 & -10 & 12\\
-13 & 5 & 1
\end{pmatrix}}
\]

