Step 1:
\begin{array}{l}

\begin{array}{l}
 \text{Find the (sample) standard deviation of the list}: \\
 (-6,8)\text{} \\
\end{array}
Step 2:
\begin{array}{l}
 \text{The }\text{standard }\text{deviation }\text{is }\text{given }\text{by}: \\
 \sqrt{(\text{variance})} \\
\end{array}
Step 3:
\begin{array}{l}
 \text{The }\text{(sample) }\text{variance }\text{of }\text{a }\text{list }\text{of }\text{numbers }X=\left\{X_1,X_2,\ldots ,X_n\right\} \text{with }\text{mean }\mu =\frac{X_1+X_2+\ldots +X_n}

model_response:
The mean is \(\bar{x}=(-6+8)/2=1\). The sample standard deviation is
\[
s=\sqrt{\frac{(-6-1)^2+(8-1)^2}{2-1}}
=\sqrt{98}
=\boxed{7\sqrt{2}\approx 9.90}.
\]

