model_response:
Let \(A=\begin{pmatrix}2&2\\-1&-3\end{pmatrix}\). Since
\[
\det A=2(-3)-2(-1)=-4\ne0,
\]
its pseudoinverse equals its ordinary inverse:
\[
\boxed{A^+=A^{-1}
=\frac1{-4}\begin{pmatrix}-3&-2\\1&2\end{pmatrix}
=\begin{pmatrix}\frac34&\frac12\\[2pt]-\frac14&-\frac12\end{pmatrix}.}
\]

