\end{array}
Step 3:
\begin{array}{l}
 \text{The }\text{(sample) }\text{variance }\text{of }\text{a }\text{list }\text{of }\text{numbers }X=\left\{X_1,X_2,\ldots ,X_n\right\} \text{with }\text{mean }\mu =\frac{X_1+X_2+\ldots

model_response:
The mean is \(\bar{x}=\frac{-11+3+1+5}{4}=-0.5\).

The **sample standard deviation** is
\[
s=\sqrt{\frac{\sum (x_i-\bar{x})^2}{n-1}}
=\sqrt{\frac{(-10.5)^2+3.5^2+1.5^2+5.5^2}{3}}
=\sqrt{\frac{155}{3}}
\approx \boxed{7.19}.
\]

