model_response:
Yes—the inverse is correct. We can verify by multiplication:
\[
\begin{pmatrix}0&-5\\2&-5\end{pmatrix}
\begin{pmatrix}-\frac12&\frac12\\-\frac15&0\end{pmatrix}
=
\begin{pmatrix}
1&0\\
-1+1&1
\end{pmatrix}
=I.
\]
Since the matrix is invertible, its Moore–Penrose pseudoinverse is the same as its inverse.

