question:
Add the two matrices
$\left(
\begin{array}{cc}
 9 & \frac{23}{3} \\
 -2 & -\frac{26}{3} \\
\end{array}
\right)$ and
$\left(
\begin{array}{cc}
 -4 & \frac{47}{6} \\
 -\frac{37}{6} & -\frac{5}{3} \\
\end{array}
\right)$

ground_truth:
Step 1:
\begin{array}{l}

\begin{array}{l}
 \text{Simplify the following}: \\
 \left(
\begin{array}{cc}
 9 & \frac{23}{3} \\
 -2 & -\frac{26}{3} \\
\end{array}
Step 2:
\begin{array}{l}
 \left(
\begin{array}{cc}
 9 & \frac{23}{3} \\
 -2 & -\frac{26}{3} \\
\end{array}
Step 3:
\begin{array}{l}
 9-4=5: \\
 \left(
\begin{array}{cc}
 \fbox{$5$} & \frac{23}{3}+\frac{47}{6} \\
 -2-\frac{37}{6} & -\frac{26}{3}-\frac{5}{3} \\
\end{array}
Step 4:
\begin{array}{l}
 \text{Put }\frac{23}{3}+\frac{47}{6} \tex

model_response:
Adding corresponding entries gives
\[
\begin{pmatrix}
9-4 & \frac{23}{3}+\frac{47}{6}\\[4pt]
-2-\frac{37}{6} & -\frac{26}{3}-\frac{5}{3}
\end{pmatrix}
=
\boxed{\begin{pmatrix}
5 & \frac{31}{2}\\[4pt]
-\frac{49}{6} & -\frac{31}{3}
\end{pmatrix}}.
\]

