Let \(A=\begin{pmatrix}4&5\\-4&0\end{pmatrix}\). Since
\[
\det A=4\cdot0-5(-4)=20\ne0,
\]
its pseudoinverse equals its ordinary inverse:
\[
\boxed{A^{+}=A^{-1}
=\frac1{20}\begin{pmatrix}0&-5\\4&4\end{pmatrix}
=\begin{pmatrix}0&-\tfrac14\\[2pt]\tfrac15&\tfrac15\end{pmatrix}.}
\]

